│ ### CAHIER DES CHARGES COMPLET (comportements attendus à vérifier)          │
│ ## Objective                                                                │
│ Create a vanilla HTML/CSS/JS interactive Bubble Sort visualizer in three    │
│ separate files (index.html, styles.css, script.js) with no external         │
│ frameworks or CDNs.                                                         │
│                                                                             │
│ ## Expected Features                                                        │
│ - **Visual Representation**: Display a table of vertical bars where height  │
│ corresponds to array values. Bars animate during the sorting process.       │
│ - **Controls**:                                                             │
│   - "Start Sort" button: Initiates a step-by-step Bubble Sort animation     │
│ with a visible, adjustable delay.                                           │
│   - "Reset" button: Generates a new random array.                           │
│   - Speed Slider: Allows the user to adjust the animation delay.            │
│   - Comparison Counter: Displays the total number of comparisons performed. │
│ - **Visual States**:                                                        │
│   - Default color for unsorted bars.                                        │
│   - Specific color for the bar currently being compared.                    │
│   - Specific color for bars that have been sorted.                          │
│ - **UI/UX**: Clean, polished design with a dark theme (high contrast).      │
│ Fully responsive layout.                                                    │
│                                                                             │
│ ## Technical Constraints                                                    │
│ - **File Structure**:                                                       │
│   - `index.html`: Contains structure and `<link>`/`<script src>` references │
│ to CSS and JS.                                                              │
│   - `styles.css`: All styling, including dark theme variables.              │
│   - `script.js`: All logic, DOM access via IDs defined in HTML.             │
│ - **Tech Stack**: Pure HTML5, CSS3, Vanilla JavaScript (ES6+). No           │
│ libraries.                                                                  │
│ - **Animation**: Use `requestAnimationFrame` for smooth rendering and       │
│ `setTimeout`/`async/await` for step-by-step control.                        │
│ - **Design**: Adhere to WCAG contrast ratios for dark mode. Use modern CSS  │
│ (Flexbox/Grid) for responsiveness.                                          │
│                                                                             │
│ ## Acceptance Criteria                                                      │
│ - Given a random array, clicking "Start Sort" triggers the algorithm        │
│ step-by-step with the selected speed.                                       │
│ - When a bar is compared, it turns [Color A]; when sorted, it turns [Color  │
│ B].                                                                         │
│ - The comparison count updates in real-time.                                │
│ - The layout adapts to smaller screens without breaking the bar             │
│ visualization.                                                              │
│ - Code is modular and follows vanilla JS best practices (no global scope    │
│ pollution).                                                                 │
│                                                                             │
│ ## To Clarify                                                               │
│ - Specific range for random array values (e.g., 1-100) to ensure visual     │
│ clarity.                                                                    │
│ - Exact hex codes for the three required bar colors.                        │
